{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793411860,"nonce":"pSjT9lhfbJGtiadNz14oK1tjSkM=","title":"Loading a snapshot module reads the whole environment even when it carries no machine code","message":"CI run 41152900468 (2381ddbb), native tests on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu and x86_64-apple-darwin: zyntax_embed tests/snapshot_bodies_are_borrowed.rs failed with \"loading allocated 39682 bytes for an image of 147711: the bodies were copied\" (the second test in the file then failed on the poisoned lock).\n\nCause: Snapshot::attach_portable_code called portable_code_allowed(), which walks std::env::vars_os() and allocates every variable, for every lowered module, including one with no machine code. GitHub runners carry a large environment; the Mac shell's was small enough to pass. Reproduced locally by padding the environment to 51 KB: 108838 bytes allocated for a 180926-byte image.\n\nFix: return before reading the environment when the module carries no code.","files":null}]}